PHP 8.5: "Using null as an array offset is deprecated" in disqus_entity_update()
and disqus_entity_delete().

When the updated/deleted entity type has no Disqus field configured,
DisqusCommentManager::getFields() returns an empty array, so key($field) is NULL.
Passing NULL to ContentEntityBase::hasField() reaches
ContentEntityBase::getFieldDefinition(), which uses the value as an array offset
and triggers the PHP 8.5 deprecation. Guard for NULL before calling hasField().

diff --git a/disqus.module b/disqus.module
--- a/disqus.module
+++ b/disqus.module
@@ -109,7 +109,7 @@ function disqus_entity_delete(EntityInterface $entity) {
   $field = \Drupal::service('disqus.manager')
     ->getFields($entity->getEntityTypeId());
   $field_name = key($field);
-  if (!$entity->hasField($field_name)) {
+  if ($field_name === NULL || !$entity->hasField($field_name)) {
     return;
   }
   $messenger = \Drupal::messenger();
@@ -181,7 +181,7 @@ function disqus_entity_update(EntityInterface $entity) {
   $field = \Drupal::service('disqus.manager')
     ->getFields($entity->getEntityTypeId());
   $field_name = key($field);
-  if (!$entity->hasField(key($field))) {
+  if ($field_name === NULL || !$entity->hasField($field_name)) {
     return;
   }

